# 🎯 PRIMEVUE FIRST - ABSOLUTE PRIORITY RULE

## 🚨 **MANDATORY: Always Use PrimeVue First!**

### **1. COMPONENTS - PrimeVue Only**
```vue
<!-- ✅ ALWAYS use PrimeVue components first -->
<Button label="Save" icon="pi pi-check" @click="save" />
<InputText v-model="username" placeholder="Username" />
<DataTable :value="items" />

<!-- ❌ NEVER create custom components when PrimeVue has it -->
<!-- Don't create <MyButton> when PrimeVue has <Button> -->
```

### **2. STYLING - PrimeFlex Only**
```vue
<!-- ✅ ALWAYS use PrimeFlex classes -->
<div class="flex justify-content-between align-items-center p-3">
  <div class="col-6">
    <h3 class="mt-0 mb-2">Title</h3>
  </div>
  <div class="col-6 text-right">
    <Button label="Action" />
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ❌ NEVER use custom CSS classes -->
<!-- Don't create .my-flex when PrimeFlex has .flex -->
```

### **3. ICONS - PrimeIcons Only**
```vue
<!-- ✅ ALWAYS use PrimeIcons -->
<Button icon="pi pi-save" label="Save" />
<i class="pi pi-user text-primary"></i>

<!-- ❌ NEVER use other icon libraries -->
<!-- Don't use <i class="fas fa-save"> when PrimeIcons has pi-save -->
```

## 🔄 **Decision Flow - Follow This EXACTLY:**

### **Step 1: Check PrimeVue Documentation**
- Search PrimeVue docs for the functionality you need
- Look for existing components, props, and utilities

### **Step 2: Use PrimeVue Native Features**
```javascript
// ✅ Use PrimeVue's built-in functionality
<Textarea resize="vertical" :autoResize="true" />

// ❌ Don't hack with CSS
// Don't use: resize: vertical !important;
```

### **Step 3: Check Existing Custom Components**
- Only if PrimeVue doesn't support it
- Use our existing custom components that follow PrimeVue patterns
- Examples: `MessageEditMode.vue`, `ChatMessageContainer.vue`

### **Step 4: ASK Before Custom Solutions**
- If PrimeVue doesn't fit AND we don't have a custom component
- Ask the user before creating new custom components
- Explain why PrimeVue doesn't work for this case

## 📋 **Common PrimeVue Components to Use:**

### **Form Components:**
- `<InputText>`, `<InputNumber>`, `<InputMask>`
- `<Textarea>` (with `resize`, `autoResize` props)
- `<Dropdown>`, `<MultiSelect>`, `<Checkbox>`
- `<Button>` (with `icon`, `severity`, `text` props)

### **Layout Components:**
- `<Card>`, `<Panel>`, `<Fieldset>`
- `<TabView>`, `<Accordion>`, `<Splitter>`
- `<Dialog>`, `<Sidebar>`, `<OverlayPanel>`

### **Data Components:**
- `<DataTable>`, `<DataView>`, `<Tree>`
- `<Chart>` (various chart types)
- `<Timeline>`, `<Gantt>`

### **Utility Classes (PrimeFlex):**
```vue
<!-- Flexbox -->
<div class="flex"> <div class="flex justify-content-center">

<!-- Spacing -->
<div class="p-3 m-2"> <div class="px-4 py-2">

<!-- Grid -->
<div class="col-12 md:col-6 lg:col-4">

<!-- Colors -->
<div class="bg-primary text-white">
```

## 🚫 **ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN:**

### **❌ Don't Create Custom Components When PrimeVue Has It:**
```javascript
// DON'T do this:
<template>
  <button class="my-custom-button" @click="$emit('click')">
    <slot />
  </button>
</template>

// DO this:
<Button label="Click Me" @click="handleClick" />
```

### **❌ Don't Use Custom CSS When PrimeFlex Has It:**
```css
/* DON'T do this: */
.my-flex-container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}

/* DO this in template: */
<div class="flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
```

### **❌ Don't Use Other Icon Libraries:**
```vue
<!-- DON'T do this: -->
<i class="fas fa-save"></i>

<!-- DO this: -->
<i class="pi pi-save"></i>
```

## 🎯 **Exception Cases:**

### **Only Create Custom Components When:**
1. **PrimeVue doesn't support the functionality**
2. **Complex business logic requires it**
3. **Integration with external libraries needed**
4. **Performance optimization required**

### **Examples of Valid Custom Components:**
- `MessageEditMode.vue` (handles edit state management)
- `ChatMessageContainer.vue` (complex chat logic)
- `UserAvatar.vue` (specific user display logic)

## ⚡ **Quick Reference:**

| Need | PrimeVue Solution | Avoid |
|------|------------------|-------|
| Button | `<Button>` | Custom button component |
| Input | `<InputText>` | Custom input component |
| Layout | PrimeFlex classes | Custom CSS classes |
| Icons | `pi pi-*` classes | FontAwesome, Material Icons |
| Modal | `<Dialog>` | Custom modal component |
| Table | `<DataTable>` | Custom table component |

## 🔧 **PrimeVue Best Practices:**

### **Use All Available Props:**
```vue
<!-- ✅ Use all PrimeVue props -->
<Button
  label="Save"
  icon="pi pi-save"
  severity="success"
  :loading="isSaving"
  @click="save"
/>

<!-- ❌ Don't ignore PrimeVue features -->
<Button @click="save">Save</Button>
```

### **Combine with PrimeFlex:**
```vue
<!-- ✅ PrimeVue + PrimeFlex -->
<div class="flex gap-2">
  <Button label="Cancel" severity="secondary" />
  <Button label="Save" severity="success" />
</div>
```

## 🎯 **REMEMBER:**
**PRIMEVUE FIRST → EXISTING CUSTOM COMPONENTS → ASK USER**

**Don't hack, don't reinvent - use the framework as intended!** 🚀